{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `marr`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added explicit `uniform(0, 1)` priors for `mean_s` and `mean_r`, matching the original bounded parameters' implicit uniform priors. Replaced the loop of row-wise multinomial likelihood statements with the vectorized built-in statement `marr ~ multinomial(pr);` so the protected top-level data variable is observed exactly once, with a plain identifier on the left-hand side and outside any loop. No data fields were added or changed; `n_occasions` remains an unprotected context input.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int n_occasions;
  array[n_occasions, n_occasions + 1] int marr;
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0, upper=1> mean_s; // Mean survival
  real<lower=0, upper=1> mean_r; // Mean recovery
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[n_occasions] s;
  vector[n_occasions] r;
  array[n_occasions] simplex[n_occasions + 1] pr;

  // Constraints
  s = rep_vector(mean_s, n_occasions);
  r = rep_vector(mean_r, n_occasions);

  // Define the cell probabilities of the m-array
  // Main diagonal
  for (t in 1 : n_occasions) {
    pr[t, t] = (1 - s[t]) * r[t];

    // Above main diagonal
    for (j in (t + 1) : n_occasions) {
      pr[t, j] = prod(s[t : (j - 1)]) * (1 - s[j]) * r[j];
    }

    // Below main diagonal
    for (j in 1 : (t - 1)) {
      pr[t, j] = 0;
    }
  }

  // Last column: probability of non-recovery
  for (t in 1 : n_occasions) {
    pr[t, n_occasions + 1] = 1 - sum(pr[t,  : n_occasions]);
  }
}
model {
  // Priors
  mean_s ~ uniform(0, 1);
  mean_r ~ uniform(0, 1);

  // Define the multinomial likelihood
  marr ~ multinomial(pr);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"marr":[[4,5,3],[3,2,4]],"n_occasions":2}","protected_variables":["marr"]}
